# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Omid Shayestehpour et al. (2023). Efficient Molecular Dynamics Simulations of Deep Eutectic Solvents with First-Principles Accuracy Using Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials.
#   Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation. doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.3c00944
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 2170a704687c2bbf...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 200 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the Deep Potential model for the reline deep eutectic
# solvent (choline chloride : urea 1:2): CP2K reference calculations, the
# primary DFTB-sampled data set and its DP-GEN extension, model and
# training settings, and the test RMSEs for two system sizes. Liquid
# structure and transport results are not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
